# Manual API walkthrough. Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or Visual Studio.
# Easier alternative: open http://localhost:5006/swagger, click "Authorize", paste a user ID.

@host = http://localhost:5006
@alex = 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@priya = 11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@sam = 22222222-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@alexMotorPolicy = 33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Demo users (public)
GET {{host}}/api/users

### No user -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/me/claims

### Alex's policies
GET {{host}}/api/me/policies
X-User-Id: {{alex}}

### Alex's claims (no reserve shown to claimants)
GET {{host}}/api/me/claims
X-User-Id: {{alex}}

### Alex submits a claim -> 201 (change incidentDate to a recent date)
# @name submit
POST {{host}}/api/claims
X-User-Id: {{alex}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyId": "{{alexMotorPolicy}}",
  "incidentDate": "2026-11-20",
  "description": "Scraped the passenger door on a car park pillar.",
  "claimedAmount": 1850.00
}

### Priya tries to read Alex's new claim -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/claims/{{submit.response.body.id}}
X-User-Id: {{priya}}

### Officer work queue: unassigned claims
GET {{host}}/api/claims?assignee=unassigned
X-User-Id: {{sam}}

### Sam picks up the claim -> InReview (run twice: second time -> 409)
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{submit.response.body.id}}/assign
X-User-Id: {{sam}}

### Sam sets a reserve
PUT {{host}}/api/claims/{{submit.response.body.id}}/reserve
X-User-Id: {{sam}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1700.00 }

### Sam settles -> Settled
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{submit.response.body.id}}/settle
X-User-Id: {{sam}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 1650.00 }

### Sam tries to reject the settled claim -> 409
POST {{host}}/api/claims/{{submit.response.body.id}}/reject
X-User-Id: {{sam}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Too late" }
